+**Taking a project away.** **Download as zip** in the same menu packs the open
+project into one zip: by default the takes the timeline shows, all footage,
+pictures and sound, or every take and export, or no renders at all. **Open a
+project zip** uploads one again, here or on another machine, and opens it as a
+project of its own. That is how to carry on with a cloud GPU that keeps no
+disk between sessions: download before the machine goes, open the zip on the
+next one. Takes left out can be rendered again, since the shots, seeds and
+settings stay in the zip. The upload goes in parts, so proxies that cap request
+size do not stop a large project.
