 |---|---|---|
 | `POST /project/{name}/rename` | `{"name"}` | The name the project shows. Its folder, which is what `{name}` in every path means, stays as it was made. Returns `{"folder", "project"}` |
 | `POST /project/{name}/duplicate` | optional `{"name"}` | A copy in a folder of its own, with its clips, takes and pictures, and no renders pending. The default name is the original's with `copy` after it. Returns `{"folder", "project"}`; 409 when the name is taken |
+| `GET /project/{name}/archive?mode=` | | The project as a zip, streamed as it is packed: `<folder>/project.json`, `<folder>/h3-archive.json` (a manifest) and its files, never its history. `mode` is `timeline` (default: the active take of each clip on the timeline, every VFX clip's active take, all footage, pictures and sound), `all` (every take and the exports too) or `none` (no renders; footage, pictures and sound stay). Takes left out are taken out of the archive's project.json too |
+| `GET /project/{name}/archive/sizes` | | `{"modes": {mode: label}, "sizes": {mode: {"bytes", "files", "left_out_takes"}}}`, before downloading |
+| `POST /archive/part?id=&offset=` | the bytes of one part | Uploads an archive in parts of at most 64 MB, in order. `id` is 32 hex characters you choose; `offset` is where the part starts, 0 for the first, which starts the upload afresh. Returns `{"have"}`; 409 with `have` when the offset is not where the upload stands |
+| `POST /archive/open` | `{"id", "name"?}` | Opens the uploaded zip as a new project, its paths pointed at its new folder, at revision 1. A name already taken gets `copy` after it. Also opens a zip of a project folder made by hand, or with `h3take_projects/<folder>/` inside. Returns `{"folder", "project", "from", "mode"}` |
